    "en":  {
               "headline":  "Strong Q3 rally erased as AI selloff pushes NET toward its 200-day EMA",
               "technical":  "Trend: NET closed at $274.96 on 2026-11-20 after a 9.46% one-day drop. That puts it below the EMA 50 ($304.12) and EMA 100 ($294.25) but still above the EMA 200 ($267.65). EMAs (exponential moving averages, trend lines that give more weight to recent prices) are still stacked 50 \u003e 100 \u003e 200, so the long-term uptrend holds while the short-term trend has broken. Momentum: MACD (12/26/9, a trend-momentum gauge) is -5.88 against a signal line of -6.80, a positive histogram of +0.92. That is a bullish crossover below zero, though Friday\u0027s slide may wear it down. RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge; under 30 is oversold, over 70 overbought) is 42.36: weak, not oversold. Volatility: price sits in the lower half of the Bollinger Bands (20-day, 2 standard deviations: $248.15–$340.33, midline $294.24). It is about 55% of the way up its 52-week range ($158.83–$370.35) and 25.8% below the high. Volume of 4.76M was only about 8% above the 20-day average, and the close was near the day\u0027s low of $271.94. Support: $267.65 (EMA 200), then about $248. Resistance: $294–$304.",
               "fundamental":  "Q3 2026, reported 2026-11-05, was Cloudflare\u0027s fastest growth in nearly four years. Revenue was $782.5M (+39% YoY) and current RPO (contracted revenue due within 12 months) rose 37%. Dollar-based net retention reached 122% vs 119% a year earlier, and about 5,000 customers now pay over $100K a year (+25%). Non-GAAP operating margin was 17.5%, free cash flow was $82.1M, and management expects GAAP profitability in Q4 2026, well ahead of its 2028 target. Guidance: Q4 revenue $845–846M (~38% growth); FY2026 $2.963–2.964B. On the AI side, active developers reached 10 million (from 7M a quarter earlier), \u0027Act 4\u0027 agent-payment products booked their first revenue, and Cloudflare signed an $11M Workers deal with an AI company. Watch gross margin: 72.4% non-GAAP, down 290 bps YoY, partly because the Workers platform runs at slightly lower margins.",
               "news":  [
                            "2026-11-05: Q3 beat. Revenue was $782.5M (+39% YoY), non-GAAP EPS was $0.38 vs about $0.34 expected, and FY2026 revenue guidance rose to $2.963–2.964B. The stock had slid to about $244.51 that day before the report, then jumped roughly 20% the next session.",
                            "Analysts after results: Needham kept Buy but cut its target to $365 from $380, and Cantor Fitzgerald kept Neutral but cut to $310 from $340. JPMorgan was reported raising its target to $375 from $350.",
                            "Earnings call (2026-11-05): management pitched Cloudflare as the \u0027agentic cloud\u0027 (a platform for AI agents). Deals included a $15.5M Magic Transit contract with a Fortune 100 cloud infrastructure provider and an $11M Workers Developer Platform deal with an AI company.",
                            "2026-11-05: Cloudflare named Christian Smith as President of Revenue, a sales-leadership change as large customers rise to 75% of revenue.",
                            "2026-11-13: Gartner named Cloudflare a Leader in its 2026 Magic Quadrant for Edge Distribution Platforms, an outside endorsement of the edge network.",
                            "2026-11-20: I found no company-specific news behind the 9.46% drop. It came the same day as a broad AI-led selloff: the Nasdaq fell about 5.3%, chip stocks fell by double digits, and the S\u0026P 500 entered a correction (down more than 10% from its peak)."
                        ],
               "caution":  "The post-earnings jump has fully reversed. The stock went from about $312 after results back to $274.96 and is now below its 50- and 100-day EMAs, during a market correction in which the Nasdaq fell 5.3% on 2026-11-20 alone. If the EMA 200 at $267.65 fails, the next levels to watch are the lower Bollinger Band near $248 and the pre-earnings level around $244.51. The valuation is still high, so NET tends to fall harder than the market when AI sentiment turns. The 290 bps drop in gross margin is also worth watching.",
               "opportunity":  "Nothing in the past 30 days damaged the business. Growth sped up to 39%, net retention improved to 122%, and GAAP profitability is guided for Q4 2026. The 2026-11-20 drop looks driven by the market, not the company: volume was only about 8% above average, the EMAs are still stacked bullishly, and MACD remains above its signal line. If the $267.65 EMA 200 holds, the larger uptrend stays intact. Moving back above $294–$304 would suggest the pullback has ended.",
               "risks":  [
                             "A wider AI-sector selloff could keep pulling down high-valuation software names like NET, even with strong results.",
                             "Gross margin pressure (72.4% non-GAAP, down 290 bps YoY) as lower-margin Workers and AI inference become a bigger share of revenue.",
                             "A daily close below the EMA 200 ($267.65) would break the long-term uptrend and open the way to about $244–$248.",
                             "Markets expect a possible Fed rate hike in December, which tends to hit long-duration growth stocks hardest.",
                             "The $2.175B in convertible notes issued in August 2026 could dilute shareholders, and competition in edge AI inference is coming from hyperscalers (giant cloud providers) and other CDNs."
